WEBVTT

00:00.980 --> 00:04.150
Pleased to meet you. My name is Rose.

00:04.540 --> 00:07.430
She looks like the daughter of 
a noble house, doesn't she?

00:07.430 --> 00:09.020
Do you think she'll make it here?

00:09.300 --> 00:13.680
Emergency patients and ones with 
external injuries can arrive at any minute.

00:14.090 --> 00:16.170
Maintain a sense of alertness 
while you work here.

00:16.170 --> 00:17.030
Yes, sir.

00:17.310 --> 00:19.240
I have a meeting to go to.

00:19.240 --> 00:22.240
Hans, please show Rose around for me.

00:22.520 --> 00:24.740
Yes, Doctor Graham!

00:25.190 --> 00:26.840
I look forward to working with you!

00:27.200 --> 00:28.470
O-Oh, yes.

00:29.330 --> 00:30.850
<i>Will she be all right?</i>

00:30.850 --> 00:33.640
<i>She seems like she'd faint 
at the sight of blood.</i>

02:06.060 --> 02:07.390
When a patient comes in,

02:07.390 --> 02:11.230
we apprentices give them a simple 
examination and inform the doctors.

02:11.800 --> 02:14.370
Then the doctor in charge of 
each case will treat them.

02:14.780 --> 02:16.890
That's the system we use here.

02:17.360 --> 02:18.900
<i>I see.</i>

02:18.900 --> 02:22.230
<i>This management system is a lot 
like the one in emergency rooms.</i>

02:23.080 --> 02:26.410
This room is for emergency 
patients with external injuries.

02:26.410 --> 02:28.350
We keep surgical tools ready here.

02:29.350 --> 02:32.580
<i>They all look like implements I've used before.</i>

02:33.010 --> 02:35.020
Um, Lady Rose?

02:36.040 --> 02:38.210
Please feel free to call me Rose.

02:38.470 --> 02:40.280
R-Really?

02:41.090 --> 02:42.100
We have a patient!

02:42.780 --> 02:44.460
Bring them here right away!

02:44.460 --> 02:45.160
Yes, sir!

02:45.610 --> 02:47.570
I'll teach you how to do an examination.

02:47.570 --> 02:48.210
Yes, sir!

02:49.490 --> 02:52.980
M-My chest... I c-can't breathe.

02:55.380 --> 02:57.920
Please bring the electric 
cardiac defibrillator!

02:57.920 --> 02:59.900
And bring Doctor Graham here!

02:59.900 --> 03:00.860
Yes, sir!

03:03.440 --> 03:04.590
<i>That's the wrong call.</i>

03:05.360 --> 03:06.960
Just hold on a little longer.

03:06.960 --> 03:08.880
We'll examine and treat you right away.

03:09.420 --> 03:12.170
<i>This is no time to run tests on his heart.</i>

03:12.990 --> 03:15.870
<i>Given his condition, before 
the doctor gets here he'll...</i>

03:18.150 --> 03:19.970
Please lend me your stethoscope!

03:20.630 --> 03:23.630
We have to hurry! Every minute, 
every second, matters!

03:24.810 --> 03:26.120
U-Use this!

03:26.120 --> 03:27.470
Thank you!

03:33.540 --> 03:34.820
<i>I knew it.</i>

03:34.820 --> 03:37.730
<i>The sound of breathing on his 
left side is growing weaker.</i>

03:39.250 --> 03:41.500
<i>His jugular vein is overly 
swollen with blood.</i>

03:42.170 --> 03:44.170
<i>This is a tension pneumothorax.</i>

03:45.350 --> 03:48.970
<i>Too much air is escaping into the chest 
and putting pressure on the heart.</i>

03:48.970 --> 03:51.100
<i>It's causing him to go into shock.</i>

03:52.290 --> 03:54.570
<i>We have to treat him immediately, or else...</i>

03:55.260 --> 03:57.600
Get disinfectant solution and 
an injection needle ready!

03:57.600 --> 03:58.590
Wh-What?

03:58.930 --> 04:00.790
Hurry! Bring me an injection needle!

04:00.790 --> 04:02.200
The thickest needle you can find!

04:02.200 --> 04:03.000
R-Right away!

04:03.630 --> 04:04.840
This is it.

04:05.110 --> 04:06.560
Thank you.

04:10.070 --> 04:11.740
Rose, what are you doing?

04:12.830 --> 04:15.380
Please hold the patient down.

04:15.380 --> 04:17.380
Huh? Right.

04:25.880 --> 04:27.120
Don't let go!

04:31.570 --> 04:32.400
<i>Just a little more.</i>

04:49.550 --> 04:52.430
Please forgive me for acting 
without permission!

04:52.430 --> 04:55.350
The situation was just so urgent...

04:55.350 --> 04:56.970
I, um...

04:57.460 --> 04:58.850
What's the patient's condition?

05:01.640 --> 05:02.760
This is...

05:04.070 --> 05:05.070
Who did this?

05:07.330 --> 05:09.760
Rose, did you do this?

05:10.110 --> 05:12.830
Yes, I did.

05:13.690 --> 05:15.210
Why did you perform this treatment?

05:15.700 --> 05:17.560
Air was escaping into his thoracic cavity.

05:17.560 --> 05:20.410
I judged that it was putting 
pressure on his lungs and heart.

05:20.410 --> 05:23.590
I used this treatment to 
release the trapped air.

05:24.580 --> 05:28.730
A pneumothorax? And a tension 
pneumothorax at that.

05:30.930 --> 05:32.210
Well done.

05:32.210 --> 05:35.510
A tension pneumothorax can lead 
to death if not treated immediately.

05:35.510 --> 05:36.650
It's an emergency case.

05:37.330 --> 05:40.680
Thanks to Rose, this patient survived.

05:41.480 --> 05:45.350
<i>Doctor Graham is famous for never 
complimenting anyone.</i>

05:46.150 --> 05:49.670
But how did you know it was 
a tension pneumothorax?

05:50.390 --> 05:54.800
The patient's sudden difficulty breathing 
made me suspect a pneumothorax,

05:54.800 --> 05:59.020
and when I used the stethoscope,
 I couldn't hear any sound from the lungs.

05:59.980 --> 06:04.070
That's something which happens when 
air blocks the transmission of sound.

06:05.000 --> 06:07.290
The patient's jugular vein 
was swollen as well,

06:07.790 --> 06:09.830
so I decided it had to be 
a tension pneumothorax,

06:09.830 --> 06:12.300
which puts pressure on the heart.

06:13.460 --> 06:15.620
Incredible! That's quite impressive!

06:16.310 --> 06:18.510
Will you tell me more about it?

06:18.510 --> 06:19.960
I'd like to hear more, too!

06:19.960 --> 06:21.900
What about the risk of hemorrhaging?

06:20.630 --> 06:25.060
<i>This young girl hasn't even been here for 
half a month yet, and she's already done this.</i>

06:21.900 --> 06:23.420
Can I ask you a few questions?

06:23.420 --> 06:25.080
It was quite an impressive call.

06:25.080 --> 06:25.670
It was.

06:25.670 --> 06:27.400
And once you'd started on it...

06:26.610 --> 06:31.390
<i>As I thought, this girl is something 
rarely seen, a true genius.</i>

06:27.400 --> 06:29.380
Will you teach me how to do it next?

06:29.380 --> 06:31.280
I'd love to know more.

06:31.280 --> 06:32.330
When will you have time?

06:33.360 --> 06:34.330
That's her.

06:34.330 --> 06:37.590
She's the one who used an injection needle 
to open a patient's chest and save him.

06:37.590 --> 06:38.810
Really?

06:38.810 --> 06:43.220
But she looks like a young noblewoman 
raised in a beautiful, happy world.

06:43.880 --> 06:46.890
<i>It's natural that they'd be suspicious of me.</i>

06:46.890 --> 06:50.970
<i>But I just can't ignore a patient 
right in front of me!</i>

06:51.900 --> 06:54.310
Miss, there's an emergency patient!

06:54.310 --> 06:55.320
I'm coming!

06:55.540 --> 06:57.500
Oh, she's so reliable!

06:57.500 --> 07:00.350
Isn't it lovely to have such a 
wonderful doctor here?

07:03.150 --> 07:06.430
People tend to be captivated 
by Rose's appearance,

07:06.430 --> 07:09.030
but what's really amazing is her skill!

07:09.530 --> 07:12.360
And not just the pneumothorax, 
her other examinations, too.

07:12.360 --> 07:17.040
I see. I see. I see that you 
really like that girl, Hans.

07:17.040 --> 07:20.030
Huh? No, I, um...

07:20.770 --> 07:24.040
I know! Why don't you invite 
her to the festival?

07:25.100 --> 07:26.040
That's a good idea.

07:26.610 --> 07:30.790
Since it only happens once a year,
 it wouldn't seem odd to invite her.

07:34.000 --> 07:38.190
No, I can't. I'm not a suitable 
match for her at all.

07:38.420 --> 07:41.810
Right. Well, she is a 
beautiful young noblewoman.

07:42.190 --> 07:45.180
It's true that I was drawn 
to her looks at first,

07:48.450 --> 07:50.210
but after seeing her like that...

07:50.830 --> 07:52.710
I can't help falling for her.

07:53.320 --> 07:56.580
About the patient with the 
dislocation earlier...

07:56.580 --> 07:59.380
I lifted their hand in the 
direction of the dislocation

07:59.380 --> 08:01.700
then rotated it away from their body to fix it.

08:02.250 --> 08:05.070
<i>She can even perform the 
Kocher technique for dislocations.</i>

08:05.510 --> 08:08.090
<i>Rose's skill isn't just natural talent.</i>

08:08.090 --> 08:10.710
<i>It's as if she's already perfected her art.</i>

08:11.310 --> 08:15.390
<i>As though she was born with medical 
skills engraved into her body...</i>

08:16.930 --> 08:19.610
Doctor, is something wrong?

08:19.610 --> 08:22.090
Huh? No, it's nothing.

08:22.780 --> 08:24.850
<i>What am I thinking?</i>

08:27.000 --> 08:30.350
Oh, that's right. Today is the festival.

08:30.580 --> 08:32.030
The festival?

08:32.030 --> 08:32.870
Yes.

08:33.430 --> 08:36.200
It happens once a year. 
One of our few pleasures.

08:36.780 --> 08:38.350
Even those stationed in 
the aid center...

08:38.720 --> 08:41.580
This is the one day when most head 
straight home instead of working overtime.

08:46.930 --> 08:49.880
You should wrap up your work 
early and go see it, too.

08:49.880 --> 08:52.100
You've experienced a lot since your 
first day. You must be tired.

08:52.540 --> 08:56.260
Taking mental breaks and relaxing... 
They're both very important.

08:56.760 --> 09:00.380
Thank you for your thoughtfulness, 
Doctor Graham!

09:03.610 --> 09:05.970
Doctor Graham, we have a patient 
with a serious injury!

09:09.670 --> 09:10.980
This is...

09:16.820 --> 09:17.990
What do you think?

09:18.410 --> 09:20.740
Can his life be saved?

09:21.520 --> 09:22.810
It will be difficult.

09:23.230 --> 09:26.160
What do you mean? Explain it to me!

09:26.830 --> 09:29.360
The bullet passed through his spleen.

09:29.840 --> 09:31.690
It will be difficult to stop the bleeding.

09:32.290 --> 09:35.630
I'm very sorry, but there's 
nothing we can do.

09:46.470 --> 09:47.390
That's...

09:48.000 --> 09:49.740
the crest of the imperial family!

09:51.430 --> 09:53.360
I'll give you any reward you like.

09:53.360 --> 09:56.360
Just please save this patient,
 whatever it takes!

10:01.550 --> 10:05.380
<i>But throughout the entire empire,</i>

10:05.380 --> 10:08.340
<i>there is no method of treatment 
for a pierced spleen.</i>

10:10.910 --> 10:12.220
I'm terribly sorry, but—

10:12.220 --> 10:13.640
We understand and accept.

10:15.310 --> 10:17.250
We will do everything in our power.

10:18.130 --> 10:19.970
Rose, what are you saying?

10:26.420 --> 10:27.710
You're...

10:31.810 --> 10:33.030
<i>Elise?</i>

10:47.730 --> 10:51.170
It's a once-a-year celebration. 
Things will be lively.

10:51.170 --> 10:52.060
I see.

10:53.480 --> 10:59.470
I thought that you wanted this inspection so 
that you could see your people flourishing.

10:59.470 --> 11:03.010
No, I have some minor business 
at Teresa Hospital.

11:03.420 --> 11:06.930
I thought that you might be feeling unwell.

11:06.930 --> 11:09.630
You've seemed tired lately.

11:09.630 --> 11:12.350
And you aren't sleeping 
well at night, are you?

11:12.870 --> 11:13.880
It doesn't matter.

11:20.180 --> 11:22.390
<i>Ever since that day 15 years ago,</i>

11:23.240 --> 11:26.640
<i>I've never once had a peaceful night's sleep...</i>

11:27.740 --> 11:30.530
<i>because of that recurring nightmare.</i>

11:32.890 --> 11:36.370
Why don't you have them examine 
you at Teresa Hospital?

11:36.370 --> 11:39.660
There are many trustworthy 
doctors at that hospital.

11:40.220 --> 11:43.780
It isn't a problem. I'm already taking 
the medicine prescribed to me.

11:44.270 --> 11:45.930
I'm sure I'll recover before long.

11:45.930 --> 11:47.190
Still...

11:47.190 --> 11:50.200
This is tedious. You worry too much.

11:50.560 --> 11:53.910
It's only natural to worry 
about one's master.

11:53.910 --> 11:56.680
You take too little care of 
yourself, Your Highness.

11:58.190 --> 12:00.710
I'm lucky to have the 
subordinates that I do.

12:01.000 --> 12:05.580
And I'm fortunate to serve 
such a magnanimous master.

12:24.290 --> 12:25.090
What is it?

12:25.090 --> 12:28.190
It's just that no matter how many 
times I see Your Highness's...

12:28.190 --> 12:32.380
the Romanoff imperial family's gift of 
disguise, it strikes me as masterful.

12:32.740 --> 12:35.010
Randall, we're in the 
middle of an inspection.

12:35.010 --> 12:36.760
Watch what you say.

12:37.680 --> 12:39.330
I'm terribly sorry.

12:40.220 --> 12:42.960
You know a lot about this area.

12:43.700 --> 12:47.530
Actually, my wife gave birth 
to our son at Teresa Hospital.

12:48.130 --> 12:51.040
As I visited the hospital, I 
naturally came to know the area.

12:51.040 --> 12:53.530
I didn't know. Congratulations.

12:56.480 --> 13:00.540
This route is dark, but it will take us 
directly to Teresa Hospital.

13:09.170 --> 13:11.820
G-Give me everything you've got!

13:12.750 --> 13:15.640
If you don't want to get hurt, 
depart immediately!

13:24.290 --> 13:24.890
Randall!

13:25.960 --> 13:27.660
Randall!

13:32.310 --> 13:34.210
We understand and accept.

13:34.210 --> 13:36.050
We will do everything in our power.

13:36.050 --> 13:37.300
Rose.

13:38.290 --> 13:39.460
<i>Elise?</i>

13:39.910 --> 13:42.840
<i>She's only just started 
working at this hospital.</i>

13:42.840 --> 13:44.170
<i>What does she think she's saying?</i>

13:44.170 --> 13:46.840
The spleen has countless blood 
vessels running through it,

13:46.840 --> 13:48.760
and a bullet has pierced it!

13:48.760 --> 13:51.310
Most of the blood vessels have been severed.

13:51.310 --> 13:53.300
It's impossible to stop the bleeding!

13:53.300 --> 13:55.030
I understand that.

13:55.030 --> 13:56.780
Then what are you suggesting?

13:57.390 --> 13:59.810
We just need to remove the spleen.

14:05.000 --> 14:08.820
<i>There wouldn't be any need to stop 
the bleeding within the spleen.</i>

14:09.420 --> 14:13.040
<i>If we remove the spleen and tie 
off the blood vessels there,</i>

14:13.040 --> 14:14.370
<i>we can stop the hemorrhaging.</i>

14:14.810 --> 14:18.200
<i>It's so simple, but no one 
has thought of it before.</i>

14:18.770 --> 14:21.230
<i>This way of thinking is 
virtually revolutionary.</i>

14:21.230 --> 14:22.420
<i>But...</i>

14:23.170 --> 14:26.600
The spleen is located in the deepest 
part of the abdominal cavity.

14:26.600 --> 14:29.000
What will you do about the stomach, pancreas,

14:29.000 --> 14:30.720
intestines, and greater omentum nearby?

14:31.040 --> 14:34.410
First, I'll sever the ligaments 
supporting the spleen.

14:34.410 --> 14:37.860
Then, I believe all that needs be done 
is to rotate the position of the spleen.

14:38.650 --> 14:42.470
<i>An ordinary person like me has no chance 
of understanding what she's saying.</i>

14:43.160 --> 14:46.690
Then, who are you suggesting 
will perform this surgery?

14:46.690 --> 14:48.610
I don't have the ability to do it.

14:48.960 --> 14:50.620
Please allow me to do it.

14:52.200 --> 14:55.870
You're asking me to allow an apprentice 
to perform a surgery of this magnitude?

14:56.140 --> 14:58.860
I am aware that I am overstepping 
in asking this of you,

14:58.860 --> 15:02.890
but if he's left in this state, 
this patient will die!

15:02.890 --> 15:05.620
If we use this method to operate, 
there's a chance that we can save him!

15:05.620 --> 15:08.260
No! I <i>will</i> save him, no matter what!

15:09.560 --> 15:11.510
Can you really do it?

15:11.780 --> 15:15.520
I want to save this patient! 
Please, trust me!

15:18.980 --> 15:22.020
Very well. Make sure you save him.

15:25.610 --> 15:30.150
If we're going to perform surgery, we'll 
need one more person to act as assistant.

15:30.540 --> 15:33.640
Everyone else is busy with other patients.

15:33.640 --> 15:35.620
Even if we send an urgent summons...

15:35.930 --> 15:37.690
Then I will help.

15:37.690 --> 15:38.250
What?

15:38.820 --> 15:40.010
But, sir...

15:40.010 --> 15:44.990
Two years ago in the Angelie War, I had 
to perform various medical procedures.

15:45.480 --> 15:47.000
I should prove helpful.

15:49.910 --> 15:51.520
Then, um, Lord...

15:51.800 --> 15:54.010
Please call me Ron.

15:54.400 --> 15:56.950
As you wish, Lord Ron.

15:59.910 --> 16:03.110
<i>His condition suggests that the 
damage to the spleen is severe.</i>

16:03.110 --> 16:05.510
<i>Even with surgery, he's quite likely to die.</i>

16:06.330 --> 16:09.910
<i>Even from the perspective of 
my past life, this is a serious case.</i>

16:09.910 --> 16:12.500
<i>I can't let my focus waver 
for a single moment.</i>

16:14.110 --> 16:15.700
Now, I will begin.

16:18.720 --> 16:20.400
<i>The bleeding is severe.</i>

16:20.910 --> 16:24.830
Lord Ron, use gauze to apply 
pressure and limit the bleed area!

16:24.830 --> 16:26.550
Use as much gauze as you can!

16:26.550 --> 16:27.530
Understood.

16:28.160 --> 16:29.480
Doctor Graham,

16:29.480 --> 16:33.140
use this instrument to move the stomach
 and intestines toward me a little.

16:33.860 --> 16:36.230
At the same time, lift the ribs.

16:36.230 --> 16:37.390
All right.

16:38.890 --> 16:43.440
<i>She isn't hesitating at all. It's as though 
she's done this surgery countless times.</i>

16:44.690 --> 16:47.010
What should I do next?

16:47.420 --> 16:49.100
I will now remove the spleen.

16:49.640 --> 16:53.400
If we detach the spleen from where it's 
connected to the pancreas behind it,

16:53.400 --> 16:56.340
the spleen will come away, and 
we'll be able to remove it.

16:57.150 --> 17:01.390
<i>If she can do this as envisioned, 
removing the spleen is possible.</i>

17:02.350 --> 17:05.070
<i>But that's only </i>if<i> she can do it...</i>

17:05.070 --> 17:06.620
<i>if Rose can do it.</i>

17:07.330 --> 17:08.720
Doctor Graham.

17:09.720 --> 17:11.490
I can do this!

17:11.490 --> 17:16.020
If you will trust me, doctor, 
we will save this patient!

17:17.490 --> 17:18.570
All right.

17:24.850 --> 17:28.570
<i>I'm not well-versed in medicine, but her 
handling of the tools shows she's the real thing.</i>

17:29.260 --> 17:33.240
<i>My father's presence is absolute 
in his dominion over this empire.</i>

17:33.240 --> 17:37.520
<i>The moment he wished for it, 
our engagement was all but finalized.</i>

17:37.520 --> 17:42.630
<i>But Elise straightforwardly defied my 
father in an attempt to become a doctor.</i>

17:42.940 --> 17:46.640
<i>I had thought that I didn't care 
who my fiancée was, but...</i>

17:51.320 --> 17:53.590
The surgery on the affected 
area is now complete.

17:53.910 --> 17:55.330
<i>It was perfect.</i>

17:55.330 --> 17:57.720
<i>It was just like being in a dream.</i>

18:07.590 --> 18:08.730
Lord Ron?

18:09.870 --> 18:14.480
The surgery ended successfully. 
I believe he will recover with time.

18:14.480 --> 18:16.120
Allow me to thank you once more.

18:16.350 --> 18:20.080
Not at all. It's all thanks 
to your assistance, Lord Ron.

18:20.080 --> 18:22.040
You did truly good work today.

18:22.370 --> 18:25.790
I only did what should be done.

18:26.180 --> 18:28.790
Regarding the reward I promised,

18:28.790 --> 18:31.540
tell me what you want. Anything you wish.

18:31.540 --> 18:33.390
You shouldn't be saying that to me,

18:33.390 --> 18:35.480
but to the hospital's accountants.

18:35.790 --> 18:39.740
After all, I'm the one who only 
did what I should as a doctor.

18:40.320 --> 18:43.490
I'm sure you'll be shocked 
when you see the bill.

18:43.490 --> 18:49.000
At this hospital, the commoners and 
nobility are charged different sums.

18:49.000 --> 18:53.180
Please don't be angry later if you 
think you've been overcharged.

18:54.530 --> 18:56.180
Then, I'll take my leave.

18:57.210 --> 18:58.430
Lord Ron?

18:59.460 --> 19:02.190
I'm all right. No need to worry.

19:02.480 --> 19:04.500
You look pale.

19:04.910 --> 19:07.440
May I check your temperature?

19:08.760 --> 19:10.640
I-I'm perfectly fine!

19:11.760 --> 19:14.470
I experience this level of 
dizziness all the time.

19:14.890 --> 19:19.250
If you experience dizziness regularly, 
it may indicate something else.

19:19.250 --> 19:21.380
It won't take up much of your time.

19:21.380 --> 19:23.970
Won't you allow someone to examine you?

19:23.970 --> 19:26.930
Don't worry about me! Worry about Randall!

19:26.930 --> 19:30.340
I'd like to transfer him to the 
Imperial Cross Hospital tomorrow.

19:30.340 --> 19:31.310
Will that be all right?

19:31.700 --> 19:33.970
Yes, I don't think it will be a problem.

19:34.240 --> 19:36.980
I'll send the surgery report, too.

19:37.990 --> 19:42.030
<i>A splenectomy is still an 
unfamiliar surgery for them,</i>

19:42.030 --> 19:45.140
<i>so I'll have to be as detailed as possible 
in describing the procedure.</i>

19:46.000 --> 19:47.320
Please do. Thank you.

19:47.970 --> 19:53.780
Lord Ron! If your symptoms persist, 
please come back to the hospital!

20:02.840 --> 20:05.140
I was really worried, you know?

20:05.140 --> 20:05.890
I'm so sorry.

20:05.890 --> 20:07.180
Are you all right now?

20:07.180 --> 20:07.830
Yes.

20:09.300 --> 20:13.640
Doctor, here is the report on 
the recent splenectomy.

20:13.920 --> 20:14.790
Thanks.

20:17.720 --> 20:19.000
Is something wrong?

20:19.000 --> 20:19.720
It's just...

20:22.810 --> 20:24.370
<i>Her handwriting is appalling.</i>

20:24.950 --> 20:26.710
<i>Is this the handwriting of a genius?</i>

20:27.600 --> 20:30.560
<i>Is she testing me because I'm 
just an ordinary person?</i>

20:32.120 --> 20:36.350
What is this awful handwriting?
 It looks like a child's scribblings.

20:36.350 --> 20:38.630
Forget that! Hurry up and read it!

20:40.130 --> 20:43.060
What do you think? A splenectomy!

20:43.060 --> 20:45.580
It's truly a miraculous 
surgery, don't you think?

20:47.920 --> 20:50.100
It has to be a lie.

20:51.250 --> 20:53.560
I'll acknowledge the strength of the theory,

20:53.560 --> 20:55.850
but a surgery like this 
simply isn't possible.

20:56.210 --> 21:00.360
I don't know who wrote this, 
but it's all just a clever fantasy.

21:01.110 --> 21:03.100
It's no fantasy!

21:03.620 --> 21:07.570
That patient is at the Imperial 
Cross Hospital where I work!

21:07.570 --> 21:12.010
And despite the fact that his spleen was 
pierced by a bullet, he's still alive!

21:12.370 --> 21:14.140
That's ridiculous.

21:14.140 --> 21:18.900
And this patient was transferred 
from your Teresa Hospital!

21:19.830 --> 21:24.260
Who is it? Which doctor performed 
this miraculous surgery?

21:24.960 --> 21:28.340
Transferred to Imperial Cross Hospital?

21:28.340 --> 21:31.600
Could this patient's name be Randall?

21:31.600 --> 21:32.800
Yes, it is!

21:33.200 --> 21:35.650
He was a patient from the 
day of the festival.

21:36.080 --> 21:39.090
That day, Professor Graham would 
have performed the surgery.

21:42.490 --> 21:43.760
Excuse the intrusion.

21:44.390 --> 21:49.990
Doctor Graham, the director is asking 
you to come to his office immediately.

21:50.380 --> 21:51.740
Has something happened?

21:52.120 --> 21:54.750
He said something about a 
surgery from the other day.

21:56.610 --> 21:57.640
All right.

21:57.640 --> 21:59.270
Rose, come with me.

21:59.270 --> 22:00.510
Y-Yes, sir!

22:06.260 --> 22:10.010
Which Way
the Wind Blows
